rewrite.prompt:
fauna_spec gives swimmers the walker judge module

src/RimMandrake/Utils/art_eval/fauna_spec.py build_spec() sets the spec's module to "flyer" or "walker" only (around line 119). A swimming creature therefore gets the walker module, and the creature template's swimmer module text never reaches the art judge. The facing-fix specs work around this by setting module "swimmer" by hand.

Expected: build_spec() picks the module with one rule, also available on its own as a public function in fauna_spec:

    module_of(flyer, thing, kind_elems, brief_plan) -> "flyer" | "swimmer" | "walker"

where flyer is the flight flag build_spec already computes, thing is the creature's ThingDef element, kind_elems is the list of its PawnKindDef elements, and brief_plan is the body_plan from the creature's departures brief (None if it has no brief). The rule:
- a flyer is always "flyer";
- otherwise a brief body_plan of "swimmer" makes it "swimmer" (some pool fish carry no swimming marker in their defs at all);
- otherwise it is "swimmer" when the race has <waterSeeker>true</waterSeeker> AND one of its PawnKindDef lifeStages has a <swimmingGraphicData>;
- everything else is "walker". waterSeeker on its own is not enough: some hoofed waders carry it.
